# What of the repo the image build may see (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the
# Dockerfile). An allowlist: the three projects the server needs and nothing else - no .git, no
# python_rl, no tests, and no local databases or secrets.
*
!Shared/
!Client/
!Server/

# Build output from the Windows machine would confuse the Linux build.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Local SQLite databases (Server/ holds a few, including a copy of the VPS one) and logs.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/logs/
